    "relatedWorkParagraph": "\\paragraph{Telecom knowledge graphs.} Knowledge graphs in this domain model the technical content of the standard or of network operation: protocol entities for security reasoning~\\cite{xie2026cellularspecsec}, product and fault knowledge~\\cite{chen2023telekg}, slice and QoS entities for explainable retrieval~\\cite{yuan2026kgrag}, typed document structure of specifications~\\cite{yang2026semrag}, metric definitions and causal chains~\\cite{kim2026telcoagent}, and ITU-T recommendations~\\cite{luo2025kg2qa}. The Release~19 telecom knowledge graph~\\cite{gsma2026telecomkg} extracts concepts, parameters, identifiers, protocols and references from the Release~19 specifications and keeps provenance to the source text chunks; it also represents the working-procedure vocabulary of TR~21.900, such as change request, CR pack and document status, as concept nodes. The process chain complements these definitions with instance records: each document's disposition and meeting, its revisions, the pack and plenary meeting that carry each CR, and the clauses the CR modifies. Section~\\ref{sec:express} places the process chain relative to these schemas.",
